# Copy to .env before the first `docker compose up`.

# The MorphDB project this instance projects into. It is written down rather than discovered because
# both the step that creates the project and the host that scopes requests to it read this file, and
# neither can wait for the other to generate a value.
#
# Any UUID will do — change it and you get a different project. Change it and keep the volume, and
# the old project is still there, unused. One instance per project: two Formbase instances sharing
# an external MorphDB need different ids, or each will project into the other's tables.
FORMBASE_MORPHDB_PROJECT_ID=0197c0de-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
FORMBASE_MORPHDB_PROJECT_NAME=formbase

# Point the instance at a MorphDB you already run instead of the bundled one. The bundled service
# still starts unless you remove it from the compose file — this only decides what Formbase talks to,
# and the project above is created on whichever MorphDB this names.
# FORMBASE_MORPHDB_URL=http://morphdb.internal:8080

# The bundled MorphDB. This is the bundle's floor rather than the compatibility pair the README
# states for embedding the engine: the start-up step creates the project under an id it chooses, and
# an earlier MorphDB generates its own instead — leaving the host scoped to a project that is not
# there. Lowering this silently breaks that step.
# MORPHDB_IMAGE=ghcr.io/iyulab/morphdb:0.10.0

# Published on loopback only.
# FORMBASE_PORT=8080
# MORPHDB_PORT=8081

# Schema intelligence — optional, like a database extension. Supply all three or none: the host
# refuses to start on half of them rather than running with an intelligence that fails on first use.
# FORMBASE_LLM_ENDPOINT=
# FORMBASE_LLM_API_KEY=
# FORMBASE_LLM_MODEL=
